1 0 0 1 36 413 Tm (CADELOOP EVENT-LOOP SOURCE REVIEW) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 399 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 36 389 Tm (STRENGTHS) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 375 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 36 365 Tm (* The architecture separates Python compatibility from Rust scheduling/reactor state, with ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 355 Tm (hot scheduling methods bound directly to the loop instance.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 345 Tm (* The tick explicitly orders corked write flushes, polling, network callbacks, a second ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 335 Tm (flush, teardown dispatch, and ready callbacks. This is a credible low-latency design.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 325 Tm (* Blocking polls release the GIL while zero-timeout polls retain it; this is sensible, ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 315 Tm (provided all zero-timeout backend paths are provably nonblocking.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 305 Tm (* Cross-thread scheduling captures context and uses a wakeup object rather than relying on ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 295 Tm (polling.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 285 Tm (* The facade covers lifecycle, task/future factories, executors, DNS, signals, async ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 275 Tm (generators, readiness, TCP, UDP, TLS, subprocess support on POSIX, and debug hooks.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 265 Tm (* Configuration validates watermarks, timeouts, limits, worker counts, and experimental RIO ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 255 Tm (opt-in early.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 245 Tm () Tj
1 0 0 1 36 235 Tm (RISKS AND DEFECTS TO INVESTIGATE) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 221 Tm () Tj
