1 0 0 1 36 755 Tm (1. Support mismatch: package metadata declares CPython 3.11 and Windows production targeting) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 745 Tm ( while Linux is a development backend. Claims must be split by OS/backend and wheel ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 735 Tm (availability.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 725 Tm (2. Alpha maturity: RIO is explicitly unvalidated and Windows subprocess pipes remain ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 715 Tm (incomplete; these materially reduce drop-in confidence.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 705 Tm (3. Private asyncio coupling: the facade uses private asyncio.events, futures, and tasks ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 695 Tm (internals. The 3.11 pin limits exposure but raises upgrade cost.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 685 Tm (4. Temporary production traces: server and native tick paths retain environment-gated/worker) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 675 Tm ( trace scaffolding tied to a Windows access violation investigation. Treat multi-worker ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 665 Tm (Windows as high risk until resolved.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 655 Tm (5. Spin defaults: a 20 us balanced spin trades CPU/energy and noisy-neighbor behavior for ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 645 Tm (latency. Benchmark CPU-seconds/request and idle CPU, not only throughput.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 635 Tm (6. Lifespan semantics: startup errors before completion are treated as unsupported lifespan.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 625 Tm ( This mirrors common auto behavior but can mask application startup defects; strict mode ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 615 Tm (would improve operability.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 605 Tm (7. HTTP specialization: native HTTP/1.1 can avoid Python parser costs, but protocol breadth ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 595 Tm (must be scored separately: HTTP/2, HTTP/3, proxy headers, trailers, disconnects, WebSocket ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 585 Tm (fragmentation, backpressure, and malformed-input behavior.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 575 Tm (8. Eager coroutine stepping: potentially valuable but compatibility-sensitive. Test ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 565 Tm (contextvars, cancellation injection, custom task factories, tracing/profiling, exception ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 555 Tm (groups, and apps that suspend at unusual points.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 545 Tm (9. GC freeze default: helpful for stable long-lived heaps, but app-dependent. Measure memory) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 535 Tm ( retention and startup object lifetime.) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 525 Tm (10. Fairness cap: ready batches are capped at 128, which helps I/O fairness; validate timer ) Tj
1 0 0 1 36 515 Tm (drift and socket starvation under callback floods.) Tj
